      ],
      "notes": [
        "Run-time results are limited to the declared positive and negative profile.",
        "Preparation uses fixed downloads; installation and checks require no network.",
        "Only immutable original downloads may be shared. A/B prefixes are independent.",
        "Host runtime libraries are checked by the original CPG ELF compatibility checker.",
        "Exact private Rust sysroot, Temurin JRE, Viper backend, and Z3 are used by prefix paths. No rustup, cargo download, host Java, or host Z3 is selected.",
        "The prefix stores a SHA-256-bound compressed runtime capsule. Each functional check verifies every original CPG member, privately expands the runtime outside the prefix, invokes the original CPG ELF compatibility checker with private library paths, executes the real five-case profile, retains evidence, and removes only the regenerable runtime expansion.",
        "The install-time outer ELF scan sees no expanded binaries; native ELF compatibility qualification is explicitly repeated after inner extraction in the functional check."
      ],
      "summary": "Supported safe-Rust fixed-array indexing and arithmetic helper contracts with overflow/panic checks enabled; official Prusti 0.3.0 compiler driver and exact nightly-2026-08-15. No unsafe, arbitrary Vec APIs, source-build, benchmark, or compiler-equivalence qualification."
